@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 230
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9A227
actor "Fan A" as A
actor "Fan B" as B
participant "Inventory\npod 1" as I1
participant "Inventory\npod 2" as I2
database "PostgreSQL" as PG
A -> I1 : POST /holds [101, 102]
B -> I2 : POST /holds [102, 103]
I1 -> PG : BEGIN; SELECT ... seats 101,102\nORDER BY seat_id FOR UPDATE NOWAIT
PG --> I1 : both rows locked by A
I2 -> PG : BEGIN; SELECT ... seats 102,103\nORDER BY seat_id FOR UPDATE NOWAIT
PG --> I2 : ERROR 55P03 lock_not_available (102)
I2 -> PG : ROLLBACK
I2 --> B : 409 + fresh availability bitmap
I1 -> PG : UPDATE ... WHERE state = AVAILABLE\nRETURNING seat_id
PG --> I1 : 2 rows (= 2 requested)
I1 -> PG : INSERT INTO outbox ...; COMMIT
I1 --> A : 201 {holdId, expiresAt = now + 5 min}
note over B, PG : <b>Without NOWAIT</b>: B waits on the lock instead. When A commits,\nPostgreSQL re-checks B's WHERE against the new row version:\nstate is HELD, so 0 rows match. B rolls back and still gets 409.
@enduml
